  "instruction": "Implement the deletion handling in `glom.mutation.Delete._del_one` so that deep deletion operations work correctly across nested target data structures.\n\nRequired behaviour:\n- Perform key, index, or attribute deletion from a given target container (`dest`) according to the operation type (`op`), target argument (`arg`), and glom `scope`.\n- Support standard Python mappings (key deletion), sequences (index/slice deletion), and generic objects (attribute deletion), as well as types registered for custom deletion handling.\n- When a deletion target does not support deletion, or the specified key, index, or attribute cannot be deleted (or is invalid / out of range), raise the appropriate glom mutation error (e.g. `PathDeleteError` or registered mutation error) consistent with glom's error handling.\n- Support sequence/iterable deletion and star broadcast operations when deletion is performed across collections.",
